BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62.00 784.00 Tm
(8. Weather values are normalised into a single Python dictionary.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62.00 769.00 Tm
(9. The user profile is converted into runtime features.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62.00 754.00 Tm
(10. The trained feels-like model is loaded from `models/feels_like.pkl`.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62.00 739.00 Tm
(11. `predict_feels_like\(\)` predicts the personalised perceived temperature.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62.00 724.00 Tm
(12. A rule-based personalisation offset is applied to account for sensitivity and) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62.00 709.00 Tm
(health profile factors.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62.00 694.00 Tm
(13. The trained health risk model is loaded from `models/health_risk.pkl`.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62.00 679.00 Tm
(14. `predict_health_risk\(\)` predicts the user-specific risk level.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62.00 664.00 Tm
(15. Safety thresholds are applied so that health-relevant weather risks are not) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62.00 649.00 Tm
(hidden by the ML model.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62.00 634.00 Tm
(16. The trained activity model is loaded from `models/activity.pkl`.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62.00 619.00 Tm
(17. `predict_activities\(\)` calculates activity suitability percentages.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62.00 604.00 Tm
(18. The backend calls `get_forecast\(city\)` for future 3-hour forecast windows.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62.00 589.00 Tm
(19. `recommend_activity_times\(\)` ranks future time slots for the user's selected) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62.00 574.00 Tm
(activities.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62.00 559.00 Tm
